## 2. Project Goals

### 2.1 Primary Goals
- [G1] Detect the user's stress, focus, and fatigue levels in real time using software-only sensors (webcam + keyboard)
- [G2] Predict stress escalation 10–15 minutes in advance using time-series ML
- [G3] Automatically trigger environment interventions (simulated in software, real via Arduino optionally)
- [G4] Display a live, beautiful dashboard updated every 500ms
- [G5] Run 100% locally — no cloud, no data leaves the device

### 2.2 Secondary Goals
- [G6] Personalize interventions using a Reinforcement Learning agent
- [G7] Show historical productivity analytics (heatmaps, correlation charts)
- [G8] Support optional Arduino hardware integration as a plug-in replacement
- [G9] Be demo-ready and impressive for a national-level hackathon audience

### 2.3 Non-Goals (Out of Scope)
- Mobile app
- Cloud sync or multi-device support
- EEG/medical-grade sensing
- Real Philips Hue integration (optional add-on, not core)

